  "headline": "Calcium chloride is not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; Hospira's product is marked To Be Discontinued since 2025-11-07",
  "headline_cites": ["D3", "E17"],
  "sentences": [
    {"text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows calcium chloride is not listed as of 2026-10-21.", "cites": ["D3"]},
    {"text": "Hospira, Inc., a Pfizer Company, has a calcium chloride injection entry with status To Be Discontinued and an initial posting date of 2025-11-07.", "cites": ["E17"]},
    {"text": "The Hospira label for NDC 00409163110 identifies a registered plant at FEI 1021343 with a last inspection classification of NAI on 2025-02-07.", "cites": ["E15"]},
    {"text": "That plant received multiple OAI classifications in 2010 and 2011 and a Warning Letter on 2010-04-12, but its most recent inspection was NAI.", "cites": ["E5", "E7", "E9", "E14", "E15"]},
    {"text": "Corvale East holds 459 syringes at 15.6 per day for 29.4 days on hand; Corvale General holds 245 syringes at 15.1 per day for 16.2 days on hand.", "cites": ["D1", "D2"]},
    {"text": "The rule-based top option is to buy from ICU Medical Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today.", "cites": ["D4"]}
  ]
}
